===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|goh|sūgan||to suck}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*sūganą}}, from {{inh|de|ine-pro|*sug-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*suk-}}. Compare {{cog|nds|sugen}}, {{cog|nl|zuigen}}, {{cog|da|suge}}.

====Verb====
{{de-verb-strong|class=2|saugt|sog|gesogen|past subjunctive=söge}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[suck]]; to create underpressure with a tube-like object such as one's mouth
#: {{ux|de|an etwas '''saugen'''|t=to suck on something|inline=1}}
